            <ArticleTitle>Posttransplant off-pump coronary bypass and laser revascularization in a Jehovah's Witness.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>434-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 57-year-old man, who had received a heart transplant 14 years earlier, underwent coronary artery bypass grafting and transmyocardial laser revascularization for left main, left anterior descending, and circumflex coronary artery disease. The procedures were performed through a left thoracotomy incision without cardiopulmonary bypass. Because the patient was of the Jehovah's Witness faith, no blood or blood products were transfused.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
